# FIXED 2026-08-29 by ADR-011: keeping the default AND a must()
# backstop now does both.  Under vet this still refuses "superadmin"
# (the must-carrying branch dies, the scalar branches die, empty), and
# standalone evaluation generates "member" -- the preferred value
# answers the meet first, and it satisfies the must().
#
# This exhibit used to pin the trade: the conjunct killed the default
# and evaluation FAILED with [aontu/disjunct_no_gen], the documented
# G1 phase-1 limit (a preference meeting a constraint in a conjunct
# did not resolve to the default).
invite: role: (*member | member | admin | owner)
  & must(member | admin | owner, "role must be one of: member, admin, owner")
